ry numbers are what they were actually paid when they got placed. Tap any short to watch. ShortsFresher to 6.5 LPA[ Shorts thumbnail: Faisal ]Faisal M.SAP FICO Consultant · TCS Shorts4 → 9.2 LPA[ Shorts thumbnail: Nikhil ]Nikhil V.S/4HANA Finance Consultant · Capgemini Shorts9 → 18 LPA[ Shorts thumbnail: Rahul ]Rahul K.Sr. SAP FICO Consultant · Deloitte ShortsFresher to 6 LPA[ Shorts thumbnail: Meera ]Meera D.SAP FICO Associate · UST [ alumni photo ]Want to talk to someone who has done it?Request an alumni call Why now Why SAP FICO, and why now. SAP retires its older ECC platform in 2027, pushing thousands of companies to S/4HANA. Every one of those migrations needs FICO consultants, so demand and pay are climbing exactly as you would enter the field. SAP ECCsupport ends 2027 thousands of companies migrating now S/4HANAruns on FICO consultants 2027ECC mainstream endsECC support ends, triggering the global migration wave. +20-30%S/4HANA pay premiumThe premium for consultants who know S/4HANA Finance. No.1Enterprise finance platformSAP leads enterprise finance. FICO sits at its core. Why it is a smart move for you Built for commerce mindsB.Com, M.Com, CA-Inter and MBA Finance fit naturally. No heavy programming. Strong, fast-rising payFreshers start Rs 4 to 7 lakh; Rs 12 to 20 lakh within a few years. Works anywhereA global standard, with GCC VAT built in for Gulf roles. Future-proof skillConfiguration and advising stay human work, even as AI automates data entry. Eligibility Is SAP FICO right for you? SAP FICO suits anyone with a finance or commerce mindset who wants a high-paying, global career in enterprise software. You do not need prior SAP experience or a coding background to start. A strong fit if you areA B.Com, M.Com, MBA Finance or CA-Inter graduateAn accounts or finance professional wanting to upskillA career switcher moving into IT and SAPA fresher targeting a well-paid first roleA working professional after a global, future-proof skill What you will needA graduate degree, ideally in commerce or financeAround 8 to 10 hours a week for five monthsBasic comfort using a computerNo prior SAP or coding experience [ counsellor photo ]Not sure you qualify?A counsellor reviews your background and tells you honestly. Free, no pressure.Check my eligibility → The full course Curriculum, projects and tools. Week-by-week structure, what past learners built, and every tool you\'ll touch hands-on. Curriculum 10 · Projects 3 · Tools 12. Curriculum 10 Projects 3 Tools 12 M01SAP & finance foundations26 hrs · Wk 1-2", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Navigating SAP GUI, SAP Fiori and the S/4HANA systemEnterprise Structure: company, company code, business areaThe Universal Journal (ACDOCA) and how S/4HANA Finance differs from ECCDocument types, posting keys and the field status conceptMini-project: configure a company code from scratch"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Do I need an accounting or finance background to learn SAP FICO?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "It helps, but it is not required. SAP FICO sits at the intersection of finance and software, so we teach the accounting concepts you need (debits and credits, GL, AP, AR) alongside the SAP configuration. B.Com, M.Com, CA-Inter, MBA Finance and accounts professionals are the most natural fit, but committed beginners do well too."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What will I actually learn in the SAP FICO course?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Financial Accounting end to end: General Ledger, Accounts Payable, Accounts Receivable, Asset Accounting and Bank Accounting. Then Controlling (cost centres, internal orders, Margin Analysis), taxes (GST, TDS, GCC VAT), FI-MM and FI-SD integration, and S/4HANA Finance with the Universal Journal and Fiori reporting."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Will I practice on a real SAP system, or just watch slides?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "You configure on a live SAP system from the first week. You will create company codes, post documents, run the Automatic Payment Program and close a month yourself. Watching configuration is not the same as doing it, and recruiters can tell the difference."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Is SAP FICO still in demand now that everything is moving to S/4HANA and the cloud?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "More than ever. SAP\'s older ECC platform reaches end of mainstream support in 2027, which is pushing thousands of companies to migrate to S/4HANA. Those migrations need FICO consultants who understand both the finance and the new platform. That is exactly what this course teaches."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What is the starting salary for a SAP FICO consultant in India?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Freshers typically start between Rs 4 and Rs 7 lakh per year, depending on the company and your skills. With a few years and an end-to-end implementation under your belt, Rs 12 to 20 lakh is common, and senior consultants and architects earn well beyond that. S/4HANA skills add a clear premium."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Which SAP certification does this course prepare me for?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "The main path is C_TS4FI_2023, the SAP Certified Associate for SAP S/4HANA Financial Accounting. We also prepare you for C_TS4CO_2023 (S/4HANA Management Accounting, the Controlling counterpart). We build the certification preparation into the course, but the official exams are booked through SAP and charged separately."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How long is the course and how much time do I need each week?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Five months, around 240 hours, across 10 modules and three capstones. Plan for roughly 8 to 10 hours a week of live sessions plus practice. The schedule is designed so working professionals and students can keep up."}}]}'
